A||N||5||Ozzy||Procuring New members to this forum...||||5||
Z||000000||Ozzy||05-29-2000||03:53 PM||||Hi Humans...<P>Just curious...How many new Fiero owners do you all come into contact with, and point to this site??<P>Recently, I met a guy at a local airport diner who has a sweet stock Burgundy '88 GT. He has owned it since new and taken really good care of it. We yakked for awhile and I told him of this site. He has participated in some web Fiero sites but has had a few negative experiences. This just reminds me how valuable this forum is! HE said he would check it out.<P>I also, finally, unloaded my '84 SE parts car yesterday...guy from Port Townsend who has previously owned a Fiero. I refered him here saying that you are all nice, helpfull folks and that I have saved time and money by being here. <P>I know there was the idea of the Forum business card...I did not follow thru as I intended. Did anyone else? I guess I'm a little selfish because although I would not deny the assets I personally have found here to anyone, I kinda like the 'smaller' fraternity that exists too.  It's pretty rare to have 1000+ individuals, with a subject core that is so subjective to personal taste & opinion, behave as mature as we do! Recent conflicts excluded, the tone remains very helpfull & friendly as I see it.<P>Anyway, just a few thoughts I wanted to share. I will continue to recommend this site to other Fiero owners who I genuinely would like to help in the future.<P>Additionally, for all you "good Joe" vendors out there...A little living proof on how effective good bussiness practices and word of mouth advertising work; I usually recommend the few of you that I have purchased goods from. I have done this based on fair treatment on your behalves and your willingness to be helpfull and courteous on the phone. This is of great value to the novice Fiero owner! There was a complete other thread on this but quickly I'll just mention the relevant folks:<P>George, Greg, Rodney, Fiero Store. There are many more of you whom I have yet to deal with but get high praise from other forum members.<P>The other thing touching my conscience is this...in light of recent 'conflicts' it makes me wonder what new potential forum members think when they open up this site and happen to read some of these "pi$$ing contest" type threads...the new impressionable Fiero owner looking for help...<P>The last thing I want to do is force my opinions and/or facts in such a way that I offend someone else. I wish not to provoke anyone to guilt trips or anything similar; just simply airing the concept.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Just as Cliff has selflessly provided his time and efforts to bring this site to us all, I find myself humbled to protect that priveledge by responding with respect and diplomacy.<P>Sorry to go on here folks. Don't mean to rant...just woke up thankfull I guess. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||Gokart||05-29-2000||09:13 PM||||I keep this saved so I can print more when I run out! <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum5/HTML/000006.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum5/HTML/000006.html</A>  I must have left at least 25-30 now. Maybe even on the same Fiero once or twice <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"> Nobody has come out and said this found this site thanks to me, but it won't stop me from leaving them!||||reg||6
Z||000002||DXR_DAD||05-29-2000||09:43 PM||||I like this card thing, and I like helping out anyone with a Fiero. This is another form of info to give to other fieroNs.<P>I hope my club (GGF) comes up with something like this (hint, hint) I know you guys are out there  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||ThatRickGuy||05-30-2000||02:02 PM||||I think this sight is great. I actually do not own a fiero (yet). But I had an offer come across, and being a big fan of pontiacs (2 early 80s grand prix's, a '76 Ventura, and my current driver a '76 Lemans) I decided it was time to look into a car that would get more then 15 miles to the gallon and give me some erginomics. So, I began researching, and with quite a bit of research, reading half the forums here, and a dedication to T-Tops, I decided to get it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> The loan should be in by the end of this week, and I'll be cruising arround in an 88 formula w/ T-Tops  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Initial investments are the engine tune up (if compression checks out) or the complete rebuild w/ a wilder cam and new chip and all the other expences. From there, it's the KYB suspention, drop springs, poly suspension, custom sterio instalation, and finally, a needed paint job. But I'd rather have a solid drive train and tunes then a fresh paint job.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I'll keep ya guys posted on how it comes along tho.<P>oh yeah, as for great forums, check out <A HREF="http://www.classicalpontiac.com" TARGET=_blank>www.classicalpontiac.com</A>  It's where I got tons of great info on the old pontiacs  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> even a little on the fieros.||||reg||14
